Since q^2+1 = (m^2+n^2)^2/(m^2-n^2)^2 is a rational square at every
fiber, hilbert(q^2+1, *, p) = +1 identically, so inv_p(alpha) = 0
for every fiber, every prime, every c in V_q(Q_p).

Reciprocity sum   sum_p inv_p(alpha) = 0   identically.

VERDICT: No Brauer-Manin obstruction from the candidate Hilbert-
symbol class alpha = (q^2+1, c^2+1) at any of the 4 BEYOND-QC fibers.

HONEST CAVEAT: This is a single explicit candidate. Br(V)_tr^{G_Q}
has dimension 0-3 over F_2 (per PICK-15). The 'right' generator
(if any) is NOT this Hilbert symbol -- it must avoid the trivializing
Pythagorean square structure.

STRUCTURAL OBSTRUCTION TO HILBERT-SYMBOL CANDIDATES:
On V_q the three quadratic forms c^2+1, c^2+q^2, c^2+1+q^2 are all
SQUARES (= f^2, e^2, g^2). Hence ANY Hilbert symbol (*, c^2+1) or
(*, c^2+q^2) or (*, c^2+1+q^2) restricted to V_q is trivial at every
prime and every local point in V_q(Q_p). All naive 'face-based'
Hilbert classes are killed by the defining equations of V_q.

This is a strong structural reason why the transcendental Brauer
class (if any non-trivial one exists in Br(V)_tr^{G_Q}) must use
MORE EXOTIC entries -- e.g. linear combinations of (e+f),(e-f),
(g+f),(g-f),(g+e),(g-e), or 2-descent classes from one of the five
elliptic factors E_ef, E_eg, E_fg, E_H+, E_H- of J(V_q).

Sanity-verification of two alternative candidates at fiber (61,38):
  At c=2: e^2 = c^2+q^2 = 42231412/5184729
  is_square(numerator)? 0
  is_square(c^2+1=5)? 0
  --> c=2 is NOT generally on V_q over Q (would need rational e).
  This confirms: V_q(Q) is constrained; alpha at a putative Q-point
  evaluates with c^2+q^2 = (rational e)^2 making it a square.

  In summary: ANY Hilbert symbol class on V_q whose second argument
  is a defining quadratic form of V_q is automatically trivial at all
  rational points -- so cannot give a Brauer-Manin obstruction.
