Conclusion: This specific candidate Hilbert-symbol class gives NO
Brauer-Manin obstruction at any of the 4 BEYOND-QC fibers. The class
is identically trivial because q^2+1 is a square for Pythagorean q.

This does NOT rule out Brauer obstruction at these fibers with a
different generator of Br(V_q)_tr. Such a generator must avoid the
structural squares (q^2+1, c^2+1, c^2+q^2, c^2+1+q^2) which all
automatically trivialize Hilbert symbols on V_q.
